WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:19.085
"Rosie!" Mom called. "We're waiting!"

2
00:00:19.086 --> 00:00:23.215
Rosie was juggling some tennis balls.

3
00:00:23.216 --> 00:00:30.081
"Coming!" she answered.

4
00:00:30.082 --> 00:00:33.932
Rosie's brother Zack had a piano lesson today.

5
00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:39.346
After that, their brother Jimmy had a baseball game.

6
00:00:39.347 --> 00:00:42.402
"Hmm," thought Rosie.

7
00:00:42.403 --> 00:00:45.262
"It'll be a long morning.

8
00:00:45.263 --> 00:00:49.318
Maybe I can practice during the boys' activities."

9
00:00:49.319 --> 00:00:51.992
She put the balls in her backpack.

10
00:00:51.993 --> 00:00:59.844
Then she ran outside to the car.

11
00:00:59.845 --> 00:01:05.192
Zack was annoyed. "What took you so long, Rosie?"

12
00:01:05.193 --> 00:01:09.526
"I know what she was doing," Jimmy said.

13
00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:14.128
"She was practicing again."

14
00:01:14.129 --> 00:01:16.837
Zack laughed.

15
00:01:16.838 --> 00:01:19.776
"Rosie, you can't even catch one ball!

16
00:01:19.777 --> 00:01:22.884
You'll never learn how to juggle!"

17
00:01:22.885 --> 00:01:26.075
Rosie's cheeks turned pink.

18
00:01:26.076 --> 00:01:30.370
Zack was a talented piano player.

19
00:01:30.371 --> 00:01:34.089
Jimmy was the best hitter on his baseball team.

20
00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:37.220
Rosie wanted to have a talent too.

21
00:01:37.221 --> 00:01:47.345
"I just have to keep practicing," she thought.

22
00:01:47.346 --> 00:01:50.358
Later the family was having a snack.

23
00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:53.863
Suddenly they heard a boom!

24
00:01:53.864 --> 00:01:59.797
"Thunder!" said Jimmy.

25
00:01:59.798 --> 00:02:04.288
Outside, rain poured down and lightning flashed.

26
00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:08.462
Inside, the lights flickered and then went out.

27
00:02:08.463 --> 00:02:20.294
Zack groaned. "We just lost our electricity."

28
00:02:20.295 --> 00:02:28.011
Mom went to call the electric company.

29
00:02:28.012 --> 00:02:33.578
"No TV." Jimmy sighed.

30
00:02:33.579 --> 00:02:37.361
"No computer," Zack grumbled.

31
00:02:37.362 --> 00:02:41.105
"This is so boring."

32
00:02:41.106 --> 00:02:45.569
Rosie reached into her backpack.

33
00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.525
She took a deep breath.

34
00:02:47.526 --> 00:02:54.187
She tossed one, two, three balls into the air.

35
00:02:54.188 --> 00:02:57.363
"You're juggling!" Zack cried.

36
00:02:57.364 --> 00:03:04.296
Jimmy clapped. "You did it!"

37
00:03:04.297 --> 00:03:11.290
The boys watched Rosie juggle the tennis balls.

38
00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:15.702
Then she got some oranges and juggled those too.

39
00:03:15.703 --> 00:03:20.585
"Can you teach us how to juggle?" asked Zack.

40
00:03:20.586 --> 00:03:25.885
"Sure." Rosie grinned. "I finally have a talent."

41
00:03:25.886 --> 00:03:30.019
Jimmy shook his head. "You have two talents."

42
00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.282
"Two?" said Rosie.

43
00:03:32.283 --> 00:03:34.464
"Yep," said Jimmy.

44
00:03:34.465 --> 00:03:42.715
"Juggling—and working hard!"
